    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕωθεν</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠῶθεν</span></b>  (q.v.), Adv.,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕως</span> (A)) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from morn</i>, i.e. <i>at earliest dawn</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				59d
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕ. εὐθύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					1121
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				119.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔριον ἕ</span>. to-morrow
			<i>early</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.2.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>La.</u>
				201c
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕωθεν</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				278
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τό γ᾽ ἕωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					546a22
				</span></i>
			.</div>
